<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of Three Nations</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1437–1438</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Unio Trium Nationum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of Three Nations (Unio Trium Nationum) was a pact of mutual aid formed in 1437 at Kápolna by the Hungarian nobility, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szekelys">Székelys</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> against the peasant revolt of Budai Nagy Antal, and renewed at Torda in 1438. It became the basis of Transylvania's system of estates, giving these three 'nations' political rights while excluding the Romanian majority.</p></div>
